  "title": "Humboldt and Bonpland's Latin American expedition",
  "summary": "The German naturalist Alexander von Humboldt and French botanist Aime Bonpland travelled through Venezuela, Cuba, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Mexico from 1799 to 1804, measuring and collecting widely. They canoed the Orinoco for 75 days, climbed Chimborazo in June 1802 without reaching its summit, and left from Philadelphia in June 1804.",
